**`transpose(text)`** in `transpose.py`:
1. Splits input text into lines
2. Finds the maximum line length to determine output row count
3. For each column index, collects characters from each input line (using spaces for missing positions)
4. Strips trailing spaces from each output line (don't pad right)
5. Joins output lines with newlines

